<title>JAPAN: Japan agency buys 120,000 tonnes wheat at tender.</title>
<headline>Japan agency buys 120,000 tonnes wheat at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 40,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat and 60,000 of Australian wheat in its weekly tender. All the purchases are for July shipment.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 40,000    Dark Northern Spring  20,000</p>
<p>			    Hard Red Winter	 20,000</p>
<p>			    (Protein 13.0 pct)</p>
<p> Canada     20,000    1CW			 20,000</p>
<p> Australia  60,000    Standard White	  40,000</p>
<p>			    Prime Hard		20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
